# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
/bin/

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
!coverage.go
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env files: only the example is versioned
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local Claude instructions
CLAUDE.local.md

# Editor/IDE
.idea/
# .vscode/

# Secrets and credentials: never versioned (the repository is public).
# Keys and certificates
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
# GCP credentials: service account keys, gcloud ADC, files written by the
# google-github-actions/auth action in the workspace
*credentials*.json
service-account*.json
gha-creds-*.json
# Terraform state and variables (state files hold secrets in clear text)
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfvars
.terraform/

# Local Claude settings (personal permissions, never shared)
.claude/settings.local.json

# Security audits: they describe the weaknesses of the API, kept out of the
# public repository (findings go to the issues instead)
docs/audit-*.md
